<section class="content-section"><div class="wrap page-split"><div><p class="section-kicker">THE CORE JOB</p><h2>Make stored belongings easier to locate later.</h2><p>Storage gets difficult when boxes are labelled inconsistently or people cannot remember where an item was packed. SHYFT focuses on the box-and-item finding problem: maintain a clear record of contents and the location associated with each box, then search that record when something is needed.</p><p>The quality of any storage inventory depends on consistent labels and updates. Before use, confirm current app availability, supported devices and how records are stored and shared.</p></div><ol class="page-list"><li><span>01</span><div><strong>Label boxes consistently</strong><p>Choose a clear naming convention that people in the household or office can understand.</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><strong>Record useful contents</strong><p>Capture enough detail to recognise the item later without making every entry burdensome.</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><strong>Record the storage location</strong><p>Use a location description that still makes sense after a move or room rearrangement.</p></div></li><li><span>04</span><div><strong>Update as boxes change</strong><p>Keep the record aligned with reality when items are removed or stored elsewhere.</p></div></li></ol></div></section>
<section class="content-section content-section--tint"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-heading-page"><p class="section-kicker">POTENTIAL FIT</p><h2>Who should consider SHYFT Box Finder?</h2><p>People who regularly pack, store or move boxes and want a more consistent way to remember their contents and location.</p></div><div class="page-grid"><article class="page-card"><span class="page-card__number">01</span><h3>Home storage</h3><p>You keep seasonal items, keepsakes or household belongings in labelled boxes.</p></article><article class="page-card"><span class="page-card__number">02</span><h3>Office storage</h3><p>Your team stores supplies, documents or equipment and needs a shared convention for locating boxes.</p></article><article class="page-card"><span class="page-card__number">03</span><h3>Move and reorganise</h3><p>You want to preserve a useful inventory while boxes move between rooms or storage areas.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="content-section"><div class="wrap page-split"><div><p class="section-kicker">EVALUATION CHECKLIST</p><h2>Choose a storage system people will keep up to date.</h2><p>A detailed inventory is only useful when it is easy to maintain. Evaluate the real-life habits and information you need to preserve.</p></div><ol class="page-list"><li><span>01</span><div><strong>Search terms</strong><p>Can people describe items in words they will remember later?</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><strong>Location convention</strong><p>Will the location names remain understandable to other people using the inventory?</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><strong>Shared access and privacy</strong><p>Confirm whether records can be shared as needed and which details should remain private.</p></div></li><li><span>04</span><div><strong>Device and data requirements</strong><p>Check current app availability, supported devices and how data is backed up or transferred.</p></div></li></ol></div></section>
